I agree with much of the previous (for an endurance game), except two
points: Speed boots are vastly underrated. There's nothing like
outrunning or outhitting monsters. And you don't wish for silver scale
mail as a wizard, you max your luck and wish for a (cursed) magic
marker. You can write much more than just the one scroll you need to
revgeno silver dragons, and it's perfectly safe if done in an Elbereth
cage.

Magic gloves and a helm of brilliance are unimportant. It's way better
to alchemize blessed gain ability - just collect all those healing
potions you find. In case you are aiming at the artifact combination,
the orb of fate will never destroy itself, even if you aren't at
intelligence 20.

In case you don't mind experimenting a bit with "advanced" techniques,
a ring of polymorph control, a wand of polymorph, and a (blessed)
magic marker to recharge it are a very powerful combination. For
example, you can simply xorn into the correct castle turret before the
soldiers can even gather themselves. Another example, if you awaken
the wizard with a mind blast as a master mind flayer, you get to skip
the annoyances of his tower. And of course, you can hatch silver
dragons for their scales.


